{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/news/strikes-on-daesh","content_id":"bf9f4acb-3efe-4cfd-888c-37d107e46d77","description":"Royal Air Force aircraft have completed successful strikes against Daesh in a joint operation with France.","details":{"attachments":[],"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p>Royal Air Force aircraft have continued to conduct patrols over Syria to help prevent any attempted resurgence of the Daesh terrorist movement following its military defeat at Baghuz Fawqani in March 2019. Careful intelligence analysis identified an underground facility, in the mountains some miles north of the ancient site of Palmyra. This facility had been occupied by Daesh, most likely to store weapons and explosives. The area around the facility is devoid of any civilian habitation.</p>\n\n<p>RAF Typhoon FGR4s, supported by a Voyager refuelling tanker, therefore joined French aircraft in a joint strike on the underground facility on the evening of Saturday 3 January.  Our aircraft used Paveway IV guided bombs to target a number of access tunnels down to the facility; whilst detailed assessment is now underway, initial indications are that the target was engaged successfully. There is no indication of any risk having been posed to civilians by the strike, and all our aircraft returned safely.</p>\n\n<h3 id=\"defence-secretary-john-healey-mp-said\">Defence Secretary John Healey MP said:</h3>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <p>This action shows our UK leadership, and determination to stand shoulder to shoulder with our allies, to stamp out any resurgence of Daesh and their dangerous and violent ideologies in the Middle East.</p>\n\n  <p>I want to thank all the members of our Armed Forces involved in this operation – for their professionalism and their courage.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"last-child\">They were among thousands of British personnel deployed over Christmas and New Year. This operation, to eliminate dangerous terrorists who threaten our way of life, shows how our Armed Forces are ready to step up, all year round, keeping Britain secure at home and strong abroad.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2026-01-03T22:19:37Z"}],"emphasised_organisations":["d994e55c-48c9-4795-b872-58d8ec98af12"],"images":[{"caption":null,"content_type":"image/jpeg","sources":{"s216":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d46e90e0731ae2a1415/s216_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","s300":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d468fa8f5346732690e/s300_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","s465":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d468fa8f53468995326/s465_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","s630":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d46e90e0731a983a846/s630_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","s712":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d46e90e0731a4dcff75/s712_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","s960":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d46d3bf7f618eda94d2/s960_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg"},"type":"lead"}],"political":true},"document_type":"news_story","first_published_at":"2026-01-03T22:19:37+00:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/news/strikes-on-daesh","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/news/strikes-on-daesh","base_path":"/government/news/strikes-on-daesh","content_id":"bf9f4acb-3efe-4cfd-888c-37d107e46d77","document_type":"news_story","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-01-03T22:19:37Z","schema_name":"news_article","title":"Strikes on Daesh","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/news/strikes-on-daesh","withdrawn":false}],"emphasised_organisations":[{"analytics_identifier":"D17","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","base_path":"/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","content_id":"d994e55c-48c9-4795-b872